From a4f1d9cb6afedd5599c6279e8d6235811a0640d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:44:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] feat(import): STEP sheets, solid ranges and the
 shared-edge rule on solidcore

- Sheets of a surface model mesh with their open boundary; a solid with
  faces left out lands only as an incomplete model, each face named.
- The STEP import lands one facet range for each closed solid
  (SolidRanges, project key `solids`, serde default). The slicer and the
  winding check read the solids from them.
- shared_edge::solids_touch accepts an edge that closed solids share
  along a wall; a truly non-manifold soup is still refused by name.
- Face winding notes from the file; one #1617 note for inward solids;
  the syntax locator skips resource references.
- Known-fail #2844 (thread flank count) and #2845 (face-to-face solids,
  feature graph tangent pieces).

Refs #917

